   "sources": [
    "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0000320193/000032019326000024/a8-kex991q4202609262026.htm",
    "https://www.theglobeandmail.com/business/article-apple-results-iphone-sales-john-ternus/",
    "https://www.wral.com/news/ap/9698b-apple-posts-stronger-than-expected-q4-revenue-in-first-earnings-report-for-new-ceo-john-ternus/"
   ],
   "paragraph": "A quarterly report is a scorecard compared against analyst expectations. Apple's fiscal fourth quarter, its first under CEO John Ternus, brought revenue of $114.5 billion, up 12%, against $113.39 billion expected. Earnings per share were $2.10 against $1.99 expected, including $0.05 from tariff refunds. iPhone revenue was $57.6 billion and services a record $31.6 billion, while iPad and wearables missed forecasts. The $1,999 iPhone Duo went on sale in October, so it is not in these results, and it is supply-constrained. How the market judges all this is unclear, because after-hours reports disagree: Reuters says up 0.8%, AP flat, Fortune slightly down.",
